    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19312" root="سدر" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَدَرٌ</span></b>  [see 1]. You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِى بَصَرِهِ سَدَرٌ</span>, and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَمَادِيرُ</span></b> , <i>In his sight is a confusedness, so that he
does not see well.</i> (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Some say that it signifies
<i>An affection resembling vertigo, common to a
voyager upon the sea:</i> or [simply] <i>vertigo.</i> (TA
in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بقل</span>.)

